- ActionListener – Handles button clicks, menu selections, etc.
- ItemListener – Handles changes in checkboxes, radio buttons, combo boxes.
- ChangeListener – Used with sliders, spinners, tabbed panes.
- MouseListener / MouseMotionListener / MouseWheelListener – Handle mouse clicks, movement, and wheel scrolling.
- KeyListener – Captures keyboard input.
- FocusListener – Detects when a component gains or loses focus.
- WindowListener / WindowFocusListener / WindowStateListener – Handle window events (open, close, minimize, etc.).
- ComponentListener / ContainerListener – Track changes in components or containers.
- ListSelectionListener / TreeSelectionListener – Used with JList and JTree for selection changes.
- DocumentListener – Monitors changes in text components (like JTextField, JTextArea).
- TableModelListener / TreeModelListener – For JTable and JTree model updates.
